      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 71-year-old man underwent enucleation because of intractable pain ten months after receiving helium ion therapy for a uveal melanoma. There was no clinical or ultrasonographic evidence of tumor regression but histologically the tumor appeared almost entirely necrotic."},
